tasks.description:
{query} 

Protocol: 1) Extract one or more GHSA IDs from the input. 2) For each GHSA ID, call get_osv_vulnerability_data MCP tool once with the vulnerability_id parameter set to the GHSA ID ('GHSA-...'). If given multiple GHSA IDs, gather data for all of them (batch tool calls in one step if supported; never call the tool twice for the same ID). This step is critical as it will gather the relevant vulnerability report for the further agents, make sure to perform the MCP call. 3) Parse the returned JSON exactly as-is; do not invent missing fields. 4) For each vulnerability, build a plain-text summary block that contains the most relevant information like the GHSA and CVE IDs, the package name, affected versions and other relevant information. Include the range semantics clearly: vulnerable_range_start is OSV "introduced" (null only if introduced=0) and vulnerable_range_end is the first OSV "fixed" version (do not use last affected). 5) Delegate to the SBOM CVE Matching Agent via A2A with a comprehensive natural-language handoff containing all vulnerability context. If OSV data is missing or fails, state it briefly.

CRITICAL TOOL INPUT FORMAT: When calling MCP tools, your Action Input MUST be valid JSON with proper unescaped quotes. Use regular double quotes directly in your JSON, do NOT escape them with backslashes.
Correct format: Action Input: {"vulnerability_id": "GHSA-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx"}
INCORRECT format: Action Input: {{\"vulnerability_id\": \"GHSA-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx\"}}
Always use the correct format with unescaped quotes.
